[2026-03-14T19:24:57.281Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012YG35DhWHy2wjuiQSawKM2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LMJUQoQqv1WMEVvbwpgWh5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/docs/tests.md","limit":100,"offset":50},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5052,"cache_read_input_tokens":19069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PRcctAp5FCZbp1RzMX8NKJ","session_id":"0eaeef5d-e35c-43d7-a0b9-dfed2a7c76ad","uuid":"64a3a210-10bf-461c-bc9a-f4382050a588"}
[2026-03-14T19:24:57.677Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LMJUQoQqv1WMEVvbwpgWh5","type":"tool_result","content":"    50→#### Test: Login form email input is functional on repeated use\n    51→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    52→- **Action:** User types \"wrong@example.com\", submits and gets an error, then clears the field, types \"guest@example.com\", and clicks \"Log In\" again.\n    53→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is logged in and redirected to home.\n    54→\n    55→### Component: RegisterForm\n    56→\n    57→#### Test: Register with valid name and email creates account and redirects to home\n    58→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. No user with email \"newuser@example.com\" exists.\n    59→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    60→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/auth` with name and email, stores the returned user object in Redux state, and redirects to the home page (`/`).\n    61→\n    62→#### Test: Register with empty name shows validation error\n    63→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    64→- **Action:** User types \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field but leaves the name field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    65→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made.\n    66→\n    67→#### Test: Register with empty email shows validation error\n    68→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    69→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field but leaves the email field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    70→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Email is required\"). No API call is made.\n    71→\n    72→#### Test: Register with invalid email format shows validation error\n    73→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    74→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"bad-email\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    75→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). No API call is made.\n    76→\n    77→#### Test: Register with already-existing email shows error\n    78→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. A user with email \"existing@example.com\" already exists.\n    79→- **Action:** User types \"Some Name\" in the name field and \"existing@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    80→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"An account with this email already exists\"). The user remains on the register form.\n    81→\n    82→#### Test: Register form fields are functional on repeated use\n    83→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    84→- **Action:** User fills in name and an already-existing email, submits and gets an error, then changes the email to a new unique email and clicks \"Register\" again.\n    85→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is registered and redirected to home.\n    86→\n    87→## Page: Home / Search (`/`)\n    88→\n    89→<!-- Components: SearchBar, CategoryFilter, PropertyGrid, PropertyCard, FavoriteButton, FiltersPanel, Pagination -->\n    90→\n    91→### Component: SearchBar\n    92→\n    93→#### Test: Search bar displays all input fields on load\n    94→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n    95→- **Expected:** The search bar is visible at the top of the page containing four inputs: a location text input with placeholder \"Where are you going?\", a check-in date picker, a check-out date picker, and a guest count selector. A search/submit button with a magnifying glass icon is visible.\n    96→\n    97→#### Test: Search by location filters property results\n    98→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist in \"Paris\", \"New York\", and \"Tokyo\".\n    99→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" into the location input and clicks the search button.\n   100→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where the city matches \"Paris\". Properties in other cities are not displayed.\n   101→\n   102→#### Test: Search by check-in and check-out dates filters results\n   103→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Some properties have bookings that overlap with the selected dates.\n   104→- **Action:** User selects a check-in date of \"2026-04-01\" and a check-out date of \"2026-04-05\" using the date pickers, then clicks the search button.\n   105→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that are available (not fully booked) for the selected date range. The date pickers display the selected dates in a readable format.\n   106→\n   107→#### Test: Search by guest count filters results\n   108→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist with max_guests values of 2, 4, and 8.\n   109→- **Action:** User sets the guest count to 5 and clicks the search button.\n   110→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where max_guests >= 5. Properties with fewer guest capacity are hidden.\n   111→\n   112→#### Test: Combined search with all fields filters results\n   113→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Multiple properties exist with varying locations, availability, and guest capacities.\n   114→- **Action:** User types \"New York\" in the location field, selects check-in \"2026-05-10\" and check-out \"2026-05-15\", sets guests to 3, and clicks the search button.\n   115→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties in New York that are available for those dates and accommodate at least 3 guests.\n   116→\n   117→#### Test: Clearing search fields and re-searching shows all results\n   118→- **Initial state:** User has performed a search for \"Paris\" and the grid shows filtered results.\n   119→- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n   120→- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n   121→\n   122→#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n   123→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   124→- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n   125→- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n   126→\n   127→#### Test: Check-in date picker prevents selecting past dates\n   128→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   129→- **Action:** User opens the check-in date picker.\n   130→- **Expected:** Dates before today are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected.\n   131→\n   132→#### Test: Check-out date must be after check-in date\n   133→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page and has selected a check-in date of \"2026-04-10\".\n   134→- **Action:** User opens the check-out date picker.\n   135→- **Expected:** Dates on or before \"2026-04-10\" are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected. Only dates after the check-in date are selectable.\n   136→\n   137→#### Test: Guest count selector enforces minimum of 1\n   138→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   139→- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n   140→- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set the guest count to 0 or a negative number.\n   141→\n   142→### Component: CategoryFilter\n   143→\n   144→#### Test: Category filter bar displays all property type chips\n   145→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   146→- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n   147→\n   148→#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n   149→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of various types exist (apartments, houses, cabins, etc.)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PRcctAp5FCZbp1RzMX8NKJ","session_id":"0eaeef5d-e35c-43d7-a0b9-dfed2a7c76ad","uuid":"5955957e-2aab-4417-9c91-d60571e2b4b6"}
